# Praxstack skill routing

When a request matches a skill, invoke it. Do not answer ad-hoc if a skill exists.

## Think / product

- New idea, "is this worth building" → `/office-hours`
- Lost the thread → wait-what + blank-stare; see `docs/agents/high-end-operator.md`
- Cross-functional planning → `/constellation-team`

## Plan

- Spec / ticket / backlog item → `/spec` or `/speckit-specify`
- Implementation plan from a spec, do not code → `/writing-plans`
- Technical blueprint → `/blueprint-creator` or `/spec-creator`

## Build

- Implement a slice → `/tdd` or test-driven-development (failing test first)
- Backend work → `/backend-pe` or language-specific `backend-pe-*`
- Frontend work → `/frontend-pe` or `/frontend-design-excellence`

## Review

- Diff / pre-landing → `/review`
- Live UI polish → `/design-review`
- Security / OWASP → `/cso` or `/qa-security-engineer`
- Architecture lock → `/kingmode` or `/plan-eng-review` (plan mode)
- Principal engineer checkpoint → `/principal-engineer`

## Test / ship

- Report only → `/qa-only`
- Find and fix → `/qa`
- Create PR → `/ship`

## Debug

- Broken / unexpected → `/investigate` or `/systematic-debugging`

## Praxstack-specific

- Deep architecture → `/kingmode`, `/super-mode-core`
- Teaching → `/techtutor`, `/teach-pro-max`
- Agent handoff → `/cross-agent-handoff`
- Bounded improvement loop → `/superimprove`
- Personal journal / ideas → `/chronicle`, `/idea-capturer`

Full persona catalog: `docs/agents/praxstack-personas.md`
Install/refresh: `./scripts/install-praxstack-skills.sh`
